                <pb facs="0449" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg439"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure in No. 1]</seg></opener>
                <head>Sir J. Larcom to Mr Waddington.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin Castle,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 13, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>As there appears reason to suppose that Finney’s object is really to enlist men
                    for the American army, though no proof of it has as yet been received, a Strict
                    watch will be kept on his movements.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
